/-!
# A cyclic residue source detects actual local error vanishing

The localized original restriction image is generated by the unit boundary
section. If the relative local image is finite, all actual scalar errors
vanish exactly when that unit generates the reduced boundary source.
This is a source condition, not vanishing in an ambient residual error module.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite TensorProduct
